      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice in Finance",
      "description": "St. John Fisher University Portal | Assistant Professor of Practice in Finance Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Fisher Homepage Human Resources Campus Map Assistant Professor of Practice in Finance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Required Application Materials Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching philosophy Three recommendation letters or contact information for three references Additional Materials (Requested for Finalists) Student course evaluations (for candidates with teaching experience) Official transcripts (required before appointment) Position Details Posting Summary Position Title Assistant Professor of Practice in Finance Status Non-Tenure Track Overview St. John Fisher University is an independent, liberal arts institution that provides a transformative education to approximately 3,800 undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral students each year. Across its five Schools, Fisher offers more than 40 majors in the humanities, social sciences, natural sciences, business, education, nursing, and pharmacy; 11 pre-professional programs; and master’s and doctoral programs in business, nursing, education, and pharmacy. The University’s residential campus boasts a robust living and learning community and a successful intercollegiate athletics program. Fisher is a community where all are welcome, regardless of religious or cultural background. The University continues to honor its founders, the Congregation of St. Basil, by embracing their motto, “Teach Me Goodness, Discipline, and Knowledge.” We are located in Pittsford, N.Y., seven miles outside of the city of Rochester. The campus is situated on 164 park-like acres—a beautiful setting for a warm, friendly campus community. Job Responsibilities The School of Business invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure track Assistant Professor of Practice in Finance to begin Fall 2027. This position carries a 4–4 teaching load and involves teaching undergraduate and graduate courses across multiple modalities (in-person, online, and hybrid). The School embraces a teacher‑scholar model and prides itself on a high‑touch approach. We are AACSB accredited and seek to deliver applied business learning anchored in community engagement and social responsibility. Non-tenure track faculty are expected to contribute meaningfully across teaching, and service while actively engaging with students and the broader Fisher community. The candidate will have the following responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate finance courses; assess student learning and progress. Advise and mentor students and support recruitment and retention efforts. Adopt new teaching techniques and engage students through interactive methods, experiential learning, and other innovative instructional practices. Contribute to the development and improvement of courses, programs, and School initiatives. Collaborate with faculty, staff, alumni, and the business community to advance the School’s mission. Provide service to the Department, School, University, profession, and broader community, and share expertise through scholarly or professional outlets. Education / Experience Required: Proof of permanent right to work in the US on first day of employment; no visa sponsorship available. A master’s level (or higher) degree in finance or a related field from an accredited institution. ABD candidates will be considered. Preferred: Professional experience in related fields of business. Active engagement with industry and/or professional associations. Experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. Professional certification (e.g., CFA or CFP ) and experience in working with Bloomberg terminal. Experience incorporating data analytics and AI into courses. Experience in advising students who manage an investment portfolio. Preference will be given to candidates with teaching or professional experience in one or more of the following areas: investments, derivative securities, fixed income securities, fin-tech, analytics, and corporate finance. Competencies / Skills Excellent communication skills and the ability to work effectively with diverse stakeholders. A strong commitment to teaching excellence, student advising and mentoring. Ongoing professional development in pedagogy and instructional innovation. Passion for engaging with students and a strong focus on positively impacting their professional development. Ability to connect with the business community to advance the visibility and success of the school. Proficiency in technology (e.g., AI, analytics tools, instructional technologies, etc.) Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Extended periods of sitting during lectures, meetings, and office hours; occasional standing while teaching or presenting. Moving between classrooms, offices, and campus facilities. Clear verbal communication for lectures and discussions; ability to hear student questions and engage in dialogue. Reading printed and digital materials, grading papers, and preparing presentations. Typing on a computer, handling books, and using teaching tools or lab equipment (if applicable). Supervision of Employees Work Environment Equipment to be Used Job Type Full-time Work Hours Full-time, 9-month teaching load with opportunities for summer teaching Availability and willingness to work mornings, afternoons, evenings, and weekends as necessary to fulfill job responsibilities as well as to participate in and support School of Business and University events Special Conditions for Eligibility Minimum Number of References Requested 3 EEO Statement It is the policy of St. John Fisher University to provide Equal Employment Opportunity to all employees and applicants for employment in accordance with the applicable federal, state, and local laws governing non-discrimination in employment in each locality in which the University has employees. The University does not discriminate against applicants or employees in hiring, promotion, termination or the terms and conditions of employment on the basis of race, color, religion, gender, sex, perceived sex, gender identity, gender expression, the status of being transgender, sexual orientation, national origin, citizenship, age, disability, marital status, military status, veteran status, predisposing genetic, characteristics or genetic information, arrest or conviction record, status as a victim of domestic violence, or any other characteristic protected by law. The Title IX Coordinator is the designated University official with primary responsibility for coordinating compliance with Title IX and related federal and state laws. The Title IX Coordinator, Meg Flaherty, Ph.D., can be reached by phone (585-385-8232), email ( titleix@sjfc.edu <mailto: titleix@sjfc.edu >), in-person in Campus Center 209, or outside of business hours by contacting the Office of Safety and Security (585-385-8111). Work Location 3690 East Ave., Rochester, NY 14618 FLSA Exempt Salary / Hourly Range $80,000.00 - $94,000.00 per year Note The salary range for this role is set based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to internal equity, qualifications, experience, and education. The above hiring range is one component of the University’s competitive Total Rewards package which can be viewed here Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00190P Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Open Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicant Required Application Materials Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching philosophy Three recommendation letters or contact information for three references Addition